usage: politician_mapper.py [-h] [--collect-mps] [--profile SLUG]
                            [--profile-all] [--detect-patterns]
                            [--connection-graph] [--all]
                            [--max-profiles MAX_PROFILES] [--verbose]

Map politicians and their connections using public government records

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --collect-mps         Fetch all current/recent MPs from OpenParliament
  --profile SLUG        Build comprehensive profile for a specific MP (e.g.
                        poilievre-pierre)
  --profile-all         Build profiles for all collected MPs
  --detect-patterns     Detect suspicious patterns across all profiles
  --connection-graph    Generate connection graph JSON for visualization
  --all                 Run full pipeline: collect MPs, build profiles, detect
                        patterns, graph
  --max-profiles MAX_PROFILES
                        Max number of MP profiles to build in --profile-all
                        (default: 50)
  --verbose             Enable debug logging

Examples:
  python politician_mapper.py --collect-mps
  python politician_mapper.py --profile poilievre-pierre
  python politician_mapper.py --profile-all
  python politician_mapper.py --detect-patterns
  python politician_mapper.py --connection-graph
  python politician_mapper.py --all

Workflow:
  1. Run --collect-mps to get all MP data
  2. Run lobbying_collector.py to get lobbying data
  3. Run --profile-all to build all profiles
  4. Run --detect-patterns to find suspicious patterns
  5. Run --connection-graph to generate visualization data

